WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:05.210
Hey youtubers it's Charlie. Yesterday during
my Korra trailer video I asked you all to

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:09.070
submit questions so I picked 10 to answer
in this video with one bonus question. Whenever

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:14.099
episodes start I'll be doing regular Q&amp;As
after I do review videos for episodes.

00:00:14.099 --> 00:00:17.860
It's just an easy way to follow up on something
if there's a couple of big questions that

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:22.349
aren't super clear the first time you watch
each episode. With that in mind, here's a

00:00:22.349 --> 00:00:25.080
couple of clarifications about the characters
from the trailer. I'm not going to go crazy

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:29.609
with spoilers from the leaked episodes. But
if you want to comment on them, please use

00:00:29.609 --> 00:00:30.570
the spoiler tag.

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:34.970
First off, this really is a young Lin Beifong
in Republic City. We don't know how old she

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:38.890
is exactly, only that it's in her early years
on the police force.

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:42.330
Second, this airbender is one of the new main
characters. She is from the Metal Bending

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:46.090
City but I won't say more just because she's
kind of important.

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:51.640
Third, this person is Lin Beifong's half sister.
We still don't know who either of their father's

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:56.700
were, but we can talk more about it in a future
bonus video. It means that Toph was either

00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:01.380
married to two different people, or just had
relationships that didn't turn into marriages.

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:06.270
Fourth, this isn't Ba Sing Se. It's the misty
palms oasis. All those other scenes in the

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:10.920
trailer in the desert are probably tied to
this location. Ba Sing Se is in the trailer

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:14.670
too. But it's not this place. You also see
the oasis in this part where Asami is helping

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:15.450
Korra escape.

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:17.570
There was more information about this young
airbender, but because it's super spoilery

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:18.530
I'm going to wait till after I answer questions
to talk about him.

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:22.200
There have been some newer theories that because
the second issue of The Rift comic book is

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:29.200
coming out July 16th that Nick will start
airing episodes then. Comic Con is the week

00:01:30.619 --> 00:01:33.460
after that, so they might wait till then though.
But tentatively plan on a mid to late July

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:33.569
premiere.

00:01:33.569 --> 00:01:38.340
So here we go, I don't consider any of these
answers I give to be major spoilers. But fair

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:45.060
warning if you don't want to know anything
about Korra Book 3. Question 1 - Crystal asks

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:48.289
is Toph Still Alive, Missing, Dead?

00:01:48.289 --> 00:01:53.780
One of the biggest unanswered Korra questions
ever. Nothing in the leaks or anything we've

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:59.889
heard has said alive or dead. The best info
we have is that at one point she pulled a

00:01:59.889 --> 00:02:04.159
Zuko and just became a nomad, traveling across
the world and hasn't been heard from or seen

00:02:04.159 --> 00:02:05.389
since.

00:02:05.389 --> 00:02:11.170
Because that's what the producers said about
Zuko, I think that we'll see Toph eventually.

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:15.360
And because there are young Lin Beifong flashbacks
we'll see republic city middle aged Toph like

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:17.220
we did during Korra Book 1.

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:23.940
I wonder if beifong was a police officer when
all that Yakone stuff was happening...

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:27.670
Question 2 - Alice asks How many episodes
will there be this season?

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:33.060
There are 13 episodes just like Book 2. Whenever
Nickelodeon ordered more episodes of Korra

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:37.100
way way back it brought the total number of
episodes up to 52. That includes everything

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:40.210
from book 1, book 2, book 3 and book 4.

00:02:40.210 --> 00:02:45.130
So that also implies that book 4 will be 13
episodes too, but I haven't seen confirmation.

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:48.980
Nick has been dead quiet about Korra news,
so it's unlikely that they'll order more episodes

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:50.710
after Book 4 is over.

00:02:50.710 --> 00:02:57.710
If anything, they'd do a new spinoff or a
short Korra tv movie.

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:03.220
Question 3 - Bayard asks how are there so
many new Airbenders all of the sudden?

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:08.590
So there are a couple of answers to this.
First that there are repercussions from last

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:13.300
season relating to harmonic convergence. Like
bringing more balance to both the spirit realm

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:17.890
and the physical realm makes it easier for
people to tap into their own energy.

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:24.890
The other answer I'll call Sky Bison Logic.
Last season we saw a herd of sky bison being

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:30.060
bred in seclusion. It's possible that a group
of airbenders could have been living in seclusion

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:33.390
and everyone just didn't know about them until
book 3.

00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:38.500
I've heard a few things from the leaked episodes
that kind of support this, but there's not

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:43.160
a lot of context right now. Other than people
are getting more power in combination with

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:46.760
airbenders always having been around, but
hidden somewhere.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:52.010
Question 4 - actionvids asks who's Lin Beifong's
Father?

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:59.010
Still nothing about this. It seems like most
of Lin's story will focus on her relationship

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:03.060
with her surviving family members. There is
that half sister of hers, which makes me ask

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:03.680
all kinds of new questions about who Toph
hooked up with and why it didn't last, but

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:07.100
I am curious to see if we find out who the
father of the half sister is. Like if they

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:08.540
give us that information, but still withhold
the identity of Lin's father.

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:12.440
The only reason I think they'd choose to do
that would be if her father became a bigger

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:15.600
part of the plot in book 4.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:21.919
I won't flip out if they still don't tell
us, but I think we'll have more information

00:04:21.919 --> 00:04:26.360
about other members of her family. So it will
be a little easier to guess who mystery dad

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:27.580
is.

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:32.560
Question 5 - Rose asks Will Zuko be helping
team Korra or just the White Lotus?

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:39.560
I'm choosing to think of both plots as part
of the same thing. By the end of the season

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:45.310
both will come together anyway. So even if
Zuko is off doing his own thing in the first

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:48.900
couple of episodes. Eventually he will be
working with Korra.

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:53.889
After all the Zuko dragon riding clips I started
to get a lot of Avatar Roku flashbacks, so

00:04:53.889 --> 00:04:59.110
I definitely think he'll give Korra some advice.
I'm really hoping he teaches her how to bend

00:04:59.110 --> 00:04:59.699
blue fire.

00:04:59.699 --> 00:05:01.280
Korra was so headstrong in season 1 it was
easy for her to firebend. But just like metalbending

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:01.870
it's super rare to see someone bend blue fire.
In Last Airbender they said only bending prodigies

00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:01.900
could do it like Azula.

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:05.909
Question 6 - Count Swagula says I hope we
get to see Bolin evolve from just being comic

00:05:05.909 --> 00:05:07.240
relief

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:09.520
Based on all the information that's been dumped
on the internet in the last week I think you'll

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:16.520
be pleasantly surprised with Bolin this season.
He'll always be a comedian, but I think because

00:05:17.159 --> 00:05:21.159
we're spending a lot of time in the earth
nation he'll get a much deeper character arc.

00:05:21.159 --> 00:05:27.110
It's not revealed in any of the leaked episodes
but I'm hoping he learns to Metalbend. Mako

00:05:27.110 --> 00:05:30.900
learned Lightning Bending from the triple
triads, so it only makes sense Bolin would

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:33.060
eventually learn his sub bending style.

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:37.189
Question 7 - Milan Frances asks could you
explain what the political structure is, with

00:05:37.189 --> 00:05:42.379
the President and the fire nation, earth kingdom,
air nomads and water tribe?

00:05:42.379 --> 00:05:47.419
Think of it like Game of Thrones and the Seven
Kingdoms. In westeros when the andals invaded

00:05:47.419 --> 00:05:52.009
they formed seven kingdoms. There were seven
different kings. Eventually Aegon Targaryen

00:05:52.009 --> 00:05:57.409
conquered westeros and became the one king,
all the other kings became Lords.

00:05:57.409 --> 00:06:02.629
So you know how the leader of the Fire Nation
is the Fire Lord. Originally before Avatar

00:06:02.629 --> 00:06:07.460
Aang created republic city and formed the
republic the Fire Lord was a king. Now they're

00:06:07.460 --> 00:06:12.879
just a Lord. So the term is much closer to
the truth. In case anyone wasn't sure, Zuko

00:06:12.879 --> 00:06:18.180
passed the title of Fire Lord on to his Daughter,
the mother of General Iroh we saw in season

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:19.120
1.

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:21.699
Even though none of the different leaders
are King's or Queen's anymore, in the Fire

00:06:21.699 --> 00:06:26.979
Nation and the Earth Kingdom it's still hereditary.
But the Water Tribe elects their leader and

00:06:26.979 --> 00:06:29.090
the Air Nomads really don't have a leader
other than Tenzin. I think the nomads have

00:06:29.090 --> 00:06:31.099
a much more loose political structure.

00:06:31.099 --> 00:06:36.029
Question 8 - AzureRoxe asks is there any connection
between Combustion Girl and Azula, because

00:06:36.029 --> 00:06:36.809
they look very similar?

00:06:36.809 --> 00:06:37.270
Grey Delisle is voicing the evil water bender,
but I haven't seen any confirmation that she's

00:06:37.270 --> 00:06:40.870
related to Azula. I'm not totally convinced
Azula will be in any episodes. It's like the

00:06:40.870 --> 00:06:47.180
Sokka situation in Books 1 and 2. We got Katara.
But she never said where he was or if he died.

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:48.479
She barely referenced him at all.

00:06:48.479 --> 00:06:52.150
So don't be surprised if Zuko does the same
thing. Just doesn't talk about his sister.

00:06:52.150 --> 00:06:56.469
But I expect them to reference her at some
point. Even though we never saw sokka, we

00:06:56.469 --> 00:06:59.129
did see that statue of him.

00:06:59.129 --> 00:07:03.379
Not that I'm expecting an Azula statue.

00:07:03.379 --> 00:07:08.319
Question 9 - Jack asks Is Korra still cut
off from her past lives?

00:07:08.319 --> 00:07:13.699
Yes, and from the rumors I've heard it's going
to prevent Korra from entering the Avatar

00:07:13.699 --> 00:07:19.150
State. Even during the leaked episodes supposedly
Korra doesn't enter the avatar state, even

00:07:19.150 --> 00:07:22.469
during scenes when she would normally enter
the avatar state.

00:07:22.469 --> 00:07:27.919
Like look at this giant sand shark. Don't
you think Korra would be in the avatar state

00:07:27.919 --> 00:07:29.289
if this were happening.

00:07:29.289 --> 00:07:32.490
It seems like one of the big running stories
in book 3 is going to be Korra discovering

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:39.490
how to enter the avatar state again. The producers
did an interview with the wall street journal

00:07:41.650 --> 00:07:45.789
after Book 2 finished where they pretty much
implied Korra's past lives wouldn't be coming

00:07:45.789 --> 00:07:45.900
back.

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:47.909
I think it will take all season for her to
figure out a workaround to that problem. So

00:07:47.909 --> 00:07:50.379
if we don't see her entering the avatar state,
we know why. She did learn to energy bend

00:07:50.379 --> 00:07:51.240
though. So that could be like a temporary
fix.

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:57.199
I'm hoping we get to see more energy bending
this year. I saw this crazy rumor that Avatar

00:07:57.199 --> 00:08:01.689
Aang at some point used energy bending to
create a new airbender. Like he gave bending

00:08:01.689 --> 00:08:03.830
to someone who wasn't a bender.

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:08.689
That's only something we've seen the lion
turtles do, but I guess it could be possible

00:08:08.689 --> 00:08:13.680
for an avatar to replicate it. That's just
a rumor though.

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:18.389
Question 10 - Beric asks why did they show
so many fights in the trailer if the producers

00:08:18.389 --> 00:08:22.449
said that Korra's biggest battle would have
nothing to do with her bending?

00:08:22.449 --> 00:08:27.009
That's a really good question. The best answer
I can give you is that Mike and Brian had

00:08:27.009 --> 00:08:31.719
nothing to do with making this trailer. Nickelodeon
probably did it as a result of that fake trailer

00:08:31.719 --> 00:08:37.219
that was going around. Just for clarification,
when those episodes leaked, someone cut a

00:08:37.219 --> 00:08:39.919
fan made trailer with a bunch of spoilery
stuff in it.

00:08:39.919 --> 00:08:46.040
I think that Nickelodeon was more mad about
that then the mistake that led to MundoNick

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:48.089
posting the episodes early.

00:08:48.089 --> 00:08:50.889
Mike and Brian have already talked about how
Korra's big challenge this season won't be

00:08:50.889 --> 00:08:56.209
seeing who the better bender is, it will be
way more complicated than that.

00:08:56.209 --> 00:09:03.209
The other possible reason for all the fight
scenes is that the person who cut the trailer

00:09:03.690 --> 00:09:08.250
was just a random person at the studio who
has no idea what the narrative of book 3 is

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:12.250
supposed to be. So they just see a bunch of
action scenes and think fans will get excited.

00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:16.490
And you end up with a fun looking trailer,
but one that ultimately tells a different

00:09:16.490 --> 00:09:19.920
story than what Mike and Brian are telling
with the episodes.

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:25.209
It happens with movies all the time. The trailer
will just have all the big moments in it but

00:09:25.209 --> 00:09:30.070
won't really tell you what the actual story
of the movie is.

00:09:30.070 --> 00:09:35.680
Bonus Question - Andy (no avatar) asks what
is the sub bending element to air?

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:42.680
Supposedly it's what Jinora is doing here.
She's not in the spirit world, so she's not

00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:50.300
necessarily in spirit form. I'd say the best
explanation is that 
the sub style is astral projection.

00:09:57.009 --> 00:10:01.040
Jinora is almost more spiritual than Korra
on the show, so it totally makes sense she'd

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:04.540
be the first person to learn a new sub style
of bending. When I started thinking about

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:10.110
it more I actually thought that she was using
the sub style during the book 2 finale.

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:14.290
Last year we were supposed to see the new
sub style but when no one said anything I

00:10:14.290 --> 00:10:19.490
got confused. So I'm guessing they'll clarify
astral projection in the first couple of episodes.

00:10:19.490 --> 00:10:24.959
Thanks so much everyone for submitting questions,
Book 3 is going to be awesome so I can't wait

00:10:24.959 --> 00:10:26.709
to make more Korra videos. Like I said I'm
planning on just doing them every friday or

00:10:26.709 --> 00:10:28.430
saturday. Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:10:28.430 --> 00:10:33.730
My next bonus video will probably be a breakdown
of who Lin Beifong's father might be. Also,

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:38.290
let me know if you want me to do weekly Korra
Q&amp;As and I'll keep doing them too.

00:10:38.290 --> 00:10:42.959
Right now click here to watch my breakdown
of the trailer and click here to learn about

00:10:42.959 --> 00:10:45.560
the new Legend of Zelda they showed off at
E3.

00:10:45.560 --> 00:10:50.649
Thanks for watching, see you guys tomorrow.
High Fives!

